  "text": "France’s early changes—Kolo Muani for Dembélé and Thuram for Giroud—helped stabilise the game: their pass share rose from 24.7% in the pre-change window to 55.2% afterward, but they still produced 0 shots. It was initially more control, not more danger. [[ev:sb:3869685:1378]] [[ev:sb:3869685:1379]]\n\nThe sharper shift followed Acuña replacing Di María: Argentina went from 2 shots in the preceding window to 0 afterward, while France generated 2 and dominated field tilt at 85.7%. [[ev:sb:3869685:2355]] [[ev:sb:3869685:2517]] After Camavinga and Coman entered, France’s territorial dominance eased, but their chance quality jumped from 0.147 to 0.885 xG, including Mbappé’s penalty and equaliser. [[ev:sb:3869685:2660]] [[ev:sb:3869685:2661]] [[ev:sb:3869685:2928]] [[ev:sb:3869685:2987]] These are before/after associations, not proof the substitutions caused the comeback; possession here means pass share.",
